        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Meta carousel with reviews</strong> is one of the simplest and most effective social proof formats. Each carousel card features a single customer review &mdash; screenshot or designed quote card &mdash; with a consistent visual template. Stack 3&ndash;5 reviews in sequence. The swipe mechanic creates compound social proof: each card reinforces the previous one.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>TikTok customer stories</strong> must feel native to the platform. Polished production signals &ldquo;ad&rdquo; and gets skipped. The best-performing TikTok testimonials look like organic content &mdash; filmed on a phone, natural lighting, casual delivery. The creator should speak directly to camera as if recommending the product to a friend. For <a href="/high-volume-ugc" class="text-accent hover:underline">high-volume UGC</a> production, brief creators to film multiple hook variations per testimonial.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>YouTube case studies</strong> allow longer storytelling. A 60&ndash;120 second case study ad can walk through the full narrative arc &mdash; problem, discovery, result &mdash; with enough detail to be persuasive for high-consideration purchases. These work well as mid-roll and pre-roll ads targeting audiences already in research mode.</p>
